    "teach_2": {
      "id": "teach_2",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A ratio gives equal-sized parts, not exact numbers.\n\nIf two numbers are in the ratio 3:5 and total 64, think of 8 equal parts.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_2_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_2_step": {
      "id": "teach_2_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "One part = 64 ÷ 8 = 8\n\nNumbers:\n3×8 = 24\n5×8 = 40\n\nThe ratio tells the shape; the total tells the size.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_2"
        }
      ]
    },
