    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Sometimes the gap is given as a percentage of the larger number.\n\nIf the smaller is 24 and the difference is 20% of the larger, let the larger be L.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "L − 24 = 20% of L = L/5\n\n4L/5 = 24\nL = 30\n\nThe percentage belongs to the larger number, so use that as the base.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
