        "text": "Let's work through this one.\n\nPut y=72−x: 4x−216+3x=120, so 7x=336 and x=48. The smaller number is 24.\n\nNow solve it once more using that same step.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "retry_4"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5": {
      "id": "teach_5",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Two separate linear clues often become easier when we add or subtract them.\n\nSuppose:\n2x + 3y = 72\n3x + 2y = 78",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_5_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_5_step": {
      "id": "teach_5_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Add the equations:\n5x + 5y = 150\nx + y = 30\n\nSubtract the first from the second:\nx − y = 6\n\nSo x=18 and y=12. The equations were designed to reveal sum and difference.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_5"
        }
      ]
    },
