    "teach_6": {
      "id": "teach_6",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Division with remainder is another equation in disguise.\n\n'When the larger number is divided by the smaller, quotient 5 and remainder 7' means:\n\nLarger = 5×Smaller + 7",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_6_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_6_step": {
      "id": "teach_6_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If their difference is 59, let the smaller be s.\n\nLarger = 5s+7\n(5s+7)−s = 59\n4s = 52\ns = 13\nLarger = 72\n\nThe remainder must also be smaller than the divisor: 7<13.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_6"
        }
      ]
    },
