    "teach_7": {
      "id": "teach_7",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A clue may determine a relation without determining the two exact numbers.\n\nIf 5x = 6y, then x:y = 6:5.\n\nThat ratio is fixed even though (6,5), (12,10), (18,15)... all work.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_7_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_7_step": {
      "id": "teach_7_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "So always read the target.\n\nIf the question asks 'What is x:y?', one equation may be enough.\nIf it asks 'What are x and y?', the same equation is not enough without another independent clue.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_7"
        }
      ]
    },
